{
  "id": "TT2002",
  "title": "Metalium：Tensix compute kernel 的 BF16 Tile 加法",
  "language": "metalium-compute",
  "mode": "metalium-compute",
  "time_ms": 120000,
  "content": "{\"zh\": \"# 任务\\n\\n提交一个 Metalium compute kernel（C++），在 Blackhole 的 Device 0、Tensix 核 `(0, 0)` 上完成一个 `32 × 32` BF16 tile 的逐元素加法。\\n\\n系统提供可信主机、reader kernel 和 writer kernel。你只需提交 compute kernel，不要提交主机 `main()`。可信主机在执行后读取设备 DRAM 中的完整 1024 个元素并逐个比较；只打印答案不能通过评测。\\n\\n# 输入与输出\\n\\n输入是一行 `a b`。主机创建两个 BF16 tile：第一块的全部元素为 `a`，第二块的全部元素为 `b`。测试值及其和均能由 BF16 精确表示。输出 tile 的全部 1024 个元素应该为 `a+b`。\\n\\n# Kernel 接口\\n\\n入口是 `void kernel_main()`，runtime arguments 为空。Circular buffer 分配为：\\n\\n| Buffer | 用途 |\\n| --- | --- |\\n| `tt::CBIndex::c_0` | 第一块输入 tile |\\n| `tt::CBIndex::c_1` | 第二块输入 tile |\\n| `tt::CBIndex::c_16` | 输出 tile |\\n\\n每个 circular buffer 的容量是一块 tile，page size 为 2048 bytes，数据格式为 `DataFormat::Float16_b`。\\n\\n需要初始化 compute 硬件和加法，等待输入 tile 到达，获取 tile registers，用 `add_tiles` 计算，提交并等待 registers，把结果 `pack_tile` 到输出 circular buffer，然后释放 registers，弹出两个输入并 push 输出。一个 compute kernel 源码会编译成 Unpack、Math、Pack 三个 RISC-V binary，各 API 自动在对应核上执行。\\n\\n常用头文件：\\n```cpp\\n#include <cstdint>\\n#include \\\"api/compute/eltwise_binary.h\\\"\\n#include \\\"api/compute/tile_move_copy.h\\\"\\n```\\n\\n配置为 `MathFidelity::HiFi4`，`fp32_dest_acc_en=false`，`math_approx_mode=false`。SDK 是 TT-Metalium 0.79.0，SFPI 7.83.0。无需打印内容。\\n\\n# 示例\\n\\n输入：\\n```text\\n14 7\\n```\\n输出：全部 1024 个设备结果为 `21`。\\n\\n参考：[Tenstorrent 官方示例](https://github.com/tenstorrent/tt-metal/tree/main/tt_metal/programming_examples/add_2_integers_in_compute)。\\n\\n## 性能剖析\\n\\n记录中的 Profiling 将热身后的重复主机测量与容器总墙钟时间分别显示。查看中位数、P95、样本数和抖动；若有设备 trace，可逐核心查看各 stage 的 cycles 和微秒。并行 stage 耗时不能直接相加。原始 JSON/CSV 可从记录下载。\\n\", \"en\": \"# Task\\n\\nSubmit a Metalium compute kernel in C++ that adds two `32 × 32` BF16 tiles elementwise on Blackhole **device 0**, Tensix core `(0, 0)`.\\n\\nThe system provides a trusted host, reader kernel, and writer kernel. Submit the compute kernel only, without a host `main()`. The host reads all 1024 result elements from device DRAM and compares them individually. Printing an answer does not replace the device result.\\n\\n# Input and output\\n\\nInput is one line `a b`. The host creates two BF16 tiles filled with `a` and `b`. The test values and their sums are exactly representable in BF16. Every output element must equal `a+b`; comparison is exact.\\n\\n# Kernel interface\\n\\nThe entry point is `void kernel_main()` with no runtime arguments. Circular buffers are:\\n\\n| Buffer | Purpose |\\n| --- | --- |\\n| `tt::CBIndex::c_0` | First input tile |\\n| `tt::CBIndex::c_1` | Second input tile |\\n| `tt::CBIndex::c_16` | Output tile |\\n\\nEach buffer holds one tile, has a 2048-byte page, and uses `DataFormat::Float16_b`.\\n\\nInitialize the compute hardware and addition operation, wait for both input tiles, acquire tile registers, compute with `add_tiles`, commit and wait for the registers, `pack_tile` into the output circular buffer, release the registers, pop both inputs, and push the output. The same source compiles to Unpack, Math, and Pack RISC-V binaries; each API runs on its corresponding core.\\n\\nCommon headers:\\n\\n```cpp\\n#include <cstdint>\\n#include \\\"api/compute/eltwise_binary.h\\\"\\n#include \\\"api/compute/tile_move_copy.h\\\"\\n```\\n\\nConfiguration: `MathFidelity::HiFi4`, `fp32_dest_acc_en=false`, and `math_approx_mode=false`. The SDK is TT-Metalium 0.79.0 with SFPI 7.83.0. Do not print an answer.\\n\\n# Example\\n\\n```text\\n14 7\\n```\\n\\nAll 1024 values read from device DRAM must equal `21`.\\n\\nReference: [Tenstorrent's official example](https://github.com/tenstorrent/tt-metal/tree/main/tt_metal/programming_examples/add_2_integers_in_compute).\\n\\n\\n## Profiling\\n\\nThe Profiling panel separates repeated host measurements after warmup from total container wall time. Inspect median, P95, sample count, and jitter. When a device trace is available, inspect cycles and microseconds per core and stage; parallel stage durations must not be summed. Download raw JSON/CSV from the record.\\n\"}",
